(3, 'Approach', 'What does early-morning vomiting with headache suggest?', 'Raised intracranial pressure.', 2),
(4, 'Approach', 'An infant has vomiting with fever. What must always be excluded?', 'Urinary tract infection and meningitis.', 2),
(5, 'Reflux', 'When does infant reflux peak, and when does it resolve?', 'It peaks at 4 months and resolves by 12–18 months.', 1),
(6, 'Reflux', 'How does gastro-oesophageal reflux differ from gastro-oesophageal reflux disease?', 'Reflux disease is reflux with complications: poor growth, oesophagitis or aspiration.', 2),
(7, 'Reflux', 'What is Sandifer syndrome?', 'A twisting or arching posture of the neck caused by reflux.', 2),
(8, 'Reflux', 'What is the best test for reflux?', 'A 24-hour pH-impedance study.', 2),
(9, 'Reflux', 'What is the first treatment of a "happy spitter"?', 'Reassurance, and avoiding overfeeding.', 1),
(10, 'Reflux', 'Reflux does not improve with thickened feeds. What is tried next?', 'A 2–4 week trial of extensively hydrolysed formula, for possible cow\'s milk protein allergy.', 3),
