(12, 'Reflux', 'In which position should an infant with reflux sleep?', 'Supine (on the back).', 2),
(13, 'Reflux', 'Which operation is done for severe gastro-oesophageal reflux disease?', 'Fundoplication.', 1),
(14, 'Pyloric stenosis', 'Which infant typically has pyloric stenosis?', 'A first-born boy aged 2–8 weeks.', 1),
(15, 'Pyloric stenosis', 'What is the vomiting of pyloric stenosis like?', 'Projectile, non-bilious vomiting after every feed; the baby is hungry afterwards.', 1),
(16, 'Pyloric stenosis', 'What are the examination signs of pyloric stenosis?', 'Visible peristalsis from left to right, and an olive-shaped mass during a test feed.', 2),
(17, 'Pyloric stenosis', 'What does the blood gas show in pyloric stenosis?', 'A hypochloraemic, hypokalaemic metabolic alkalosis.', 2),
(18, 'Pyloric stenosis', 'What does the urine show in late cases of pyloric stenosis?', 'Paradoxical aciduria.', 3),
(19, 'Pyloric stenosis', 'What is the test of choice for pyloric stenosis, and what are the criteria?', 'Ultrasound: a muscle thickness of 3 mm or more and a canal length of 15 mm or more.', 2),
(20, 'Pyloric stenosis', 'What does the barium study show in pyloric stenosis?', 'The string sign (and the shoulder sign).', 2),
(21, 'Pyloric stenosis', 'Is pyloric stenosis an emergency operation?', 'No. Fluids and electrolytes are corrected first.', 3),
(22, 'Pyloric stenosis', 'Which operation treats pyloric stenosis?', 'Ramstedt pyloromyotomy.', 1),
(23, 'Pyloric stenosis', 'Which antibiotics are a risk factor for pyloric stenosis?', 'Erythromycin or azithromycin given in the first 2 weeks of life.', 2),
(24, 'Pyloric stenosis', 'What are the stools like in pyloric stenosis?', 'Small and infrequent (constipation).', 2),
(25, 'Malrotation', 'How does malrotation with volvulus present?', 'Sudden bilious vomiting in a newborn who was feeding well; later, blood per rectum and shock.', 2),
(26, 'Malrotation', 'What is the test of choice for malrotation?', 'An upper gastrointestinal contrast study: the duodenojejunal flexure lies to the right of the midline, with a corkscrew appearance.', 2),
(27, 'Malrotation', 'Which operation treats malrotation?', 'The Ladd procedure, by emergency laparotomy.', 1),
(28, 'Malrotation', 'What is the long-term risk after a volvulus?', 'Short bowel syndrome.', 2),
