(23, 'GI bleeding', 'What is the commonest cause of rectal bleeding in infants and toddlers?', 'An anal fissure.', 1),
(24, 'GI bleeding', 'A child aged 2–8 years passes painless bright blood at the end of the stool. What is the likely cause?', 'A juvenile polyp.', 2),
(25, 'GI bleeding', 'A child from an irrigated farming area has haematemesis, a big spleen and normal liver function tests. What is the cause?', 'Bleeding varices from portal hypertension caused by schistosomiasis.', 3),
(26, 'Meckel diverticulum', 'What is the "rule of 2" for Meckel diverticulum?', 'It occurs in 2% of people, 2 feet from the ileocaecal valve, is 2 inches long, contains 2 types of ectopic tissue and usually presents under 2 years.', 1),
